.TH CTPOOL_WAIT 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_wait \- block until the pool is idle
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadpool.h>

void ctpool_wait(ctpool pool);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Blocks until the task queue is empty and every active task stops. It
does not shut the pool down. Every worker thread stays alive, and the
caller can submit new tasks after this call returns.

Contract: no other thread should submit a task while ctpool_wait runs.
With an unbounded queue, a submission from another thread can block
this call for ever.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool   Thread pool handle (CTPOOL_INVALID or a stale/already-destroyed handle is a no-op)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
ctpool_wait waits for the queue and for the tasks that workers run. It
does not wait for the on_complete callbacks of discarded tasks. A
ctpool_shutdown_immediate(3) on another thread empties the queue at
once, and then calls the on_complete of each discarded task, with
ran == false, on its own thread. ctpool_wait can therefore return while
those callbacks still run. Wait for the return of the
ctpool_shutdown_immediate call itself to know that every one of them
finished.

The library treats a pool that a child inherited across a fork(2) call
as idle by default. fork(2) does not duplicate the worker threads of
that pool into the child. ctpool_wait on such a pool in the child
therefore returns at once. It does not wait for progress that no worker
thread in that process can ever make.

A call to ctpool_wait on pool from inside a task is also idle by
default, and returns at once. That holds when the task runs on one of
the worker threads of pool. A call from the on_complete callback of
that task is the same. The pool still counts the task that calls among
its own active tasks until that task returns. Without this, a wait here
would deadlock the worker that calls against itself.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_shutdown_drain (3),
.BR ctpool_shutdown_immediate (3)
